  "lineage": "Venezuelan-and-Colombian-Llanos plains cattle-ranch song-and-dance tradition with characteristic 3/4-against-6/8 hemiola-and-sesquialteral rhythmic-foundation. The canonical ensemble: arpa-llanera 32-string diatonic-harp (Venezuelan) or cuatro-y-bandola small-four-string-and-mandolin variant (Colombian), maracas, and either capacho large-shaker or bass. The vocal-style features high-projected open-throat cattle-driving register with improvised contrapunteo dueling-poet improvised-verse-exchange. The corrido-joropo storytelling-narrative-form, the pasaje-joropo slower-romantic-lyrical-form, and the joropo-recio fast-virtuosic-improvisational-form comprise the canonical variants. Embedded in cattle-ranch llanero rural-pastoral culture spanning the Orinoco-river-basin grasslands of Venezuela and eastern Colombia.",
